       }
      ],
      "text": "COPD:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " for repeated exacerbations or symptoms despite optimal bronchodilators; most effective with eosinophils ≥ 150/mcL. May need to de-escalate if pneumonia develops or no response; with eosinophils ≥ 300/mcL, de-escalation is more likely to cause an exacerbation."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Fluticasone is a CYP3A4 substrate:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " strong CYP3A4 inhibitors (eg, ketoconazole) raise exposure; use caution."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Acute overdose rarely needs more than observation; chronic overdose can cause hypercorticism."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
